---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Our Editorial Method | The Good Present"
  description="How The Good Present builds useful, trustworthy gift guides around people, moments, and real routines."
>
  <article class="prose-page shell">
    <header class="prose-page__hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">About The Good Present</p>
      <h1>We would rather make one useful guide than fifty thin ones.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        The Good Present is an editorial gift guide for people who want to give with attention—not
        just search by keyword and hope.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose-page__grid">
      <aside>
        <p class="kicker">Our north star</p>
        <p>Start with the person. Respect the budget. Explain the choice.</p>
      </aside>
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Guides begin with intent</h2>
        <p>
          We publish a page only when it answers a meaningfully different question. A nursing
          graduation guide can celebrate a transition. A practical guide can focus on routines. A
          budget guide can make a firm constraint part of the editorial work. Tags alone never
          become pages.
        </p>

        <h2>Products are context, not a ranking theater</h2>
        <p>
          We do not invent ratings, discounts, stock messages, or urgency. A product may be useful
          in more than one guide, but the editorial explanation must be written for that guide's
          specific reader and purpose.
        </p>

        <h2>Useful includes knowing what to check</h2>
        <p>
          Size, workplace policy, fragrance, routine, and personal taste can matter more than a long
          feature list. Our recommendations include practical considerations so a promising idea is
          easier to evaluate before leaving for a merchant site.
        </p>

        <h2>Commercial, with the lights on</h2>
        <p>
          The initial business model is affiliate marketing. That means The Good Present may earn
          money when a reader follows a qualifying merchant link and buys something. Our
          <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> explains the boundary plainly.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
